ts (158, 189, 1736) occur before 51317, and 1010 was silent in the 600-unit pre-window buffer [50717,51316], ruling out carry-over under the 600-unit gap constraint. Structurally, 883's 2-hop neighbourhood (15 nodes, centred on hub 1209 and 1038) contains neither 1010 nor 1429, so no static path exists near the target either. 883's inbound events are attributable to the locally busy hub 1209 (11 events) rather than to any chain from 1010, and the window's large overall volume (6477 events) explains incidental co-activity. Conclusion: no genuine cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**1. No outgoing activity from 1010 in the window.** Node 1010 has exactly 1 event in [51317, 89717], and it is *inbound* (from 1429); its out-degree is 0 (steps 02, 04, 07). A cascade seeded at 1010 requires at least one outgoing event from 1010 inside the window \u2014 there is none.\n\n**2. The 1010 out-edges that do exist are all before the window.** 1010's lifetime out-neighbours are {158, 189, 1736}, and all of those out-events fall in [0, 51316] with none after 89717 (steps 09, 10, 11). Moreover 1010 had **zero** events in the 600-unit run-up [50717, 51316] (step 15), so no pre-window emission could propagate into the window under the 600-unit gap rule.\n\n**3. Structural disconnection even ignoring time (confounder control for \"connection exists statically\").** The 2-hop neighbourhood of 883 comprises only {149, 296, 356, 459, 582, 883, 971, 990, 1038, 1092, 1209, 1343, 1542, 1937, 1951} \u2014 1010 and its contact 1429 are absent (step 13). Conversely 1010's 3-hop expansion is a large component containing 158/1542/etc. but 883 appears only via unrelated hubs, not as a reachable successor of a 1010 emission. So there is no even time-ignoring path 1010 \u2192 883 within 2 hops of the target.\n\n**4. Confounder control for \"the nodes are active/popular\".** 883 does receive traffic in-window (from 1038 and 1209, step 05/08/16), and 1209 is comparatively busy with 11 events / 11 partners (step 12) \u2014 so 883's inbound events are explained by a locally active hub, not by any chain descending from 1010. The window as a whole is large (6477 events, 1922 active nodes, repeat ratio 0.03 \u2014 step 01), which makes incidental co-activity likely but is not evidence of transmission.\n\n**Conclusion: absent.** The evidence is a positive absence (no source emission at all in-window, plus structural separation), not mere lack of data.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_8980b60f\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1010, 883],\n  \"window\": [51317, 89717],\n  \"confidence\": 0.9,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Within [51317,89717] node 1010 has a single event and it is inbound (1429->1010); its out-degree is zero, so no time-respecting chain can be seeded from 1010. All of 1010's outgoing contacts (158, 189, 1736) occur before 51317, and 1010 was silent in the 600-unit pre-window buffer [50717,51316], ruling out carry-over under the 600-unit gap constraint. Structurally, 883's 2-hop neighbourhood (15 nodes, centred on hub 1209 and 1038) contains neither 1010 nor 1429, so no static path exists near the target either. 883's inbound events are attributable to the locally busy hub 1209 (11 events) rather than to any chain from 1010, and the window's large overall volume (6477 events) explains incidental co-activity. Conclusion: no genuine cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 38533, "total_output_tokens": 4463, "total_tokens": 42996, "total_latency_ms": 66613, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}